    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Pacific invitation",
          "heading": "Jake White calls on Ireland to travel to Pacific Islands",
          "body": "Speaking at the Fitzpatrick Castle Hotel, where Fiji have been based this week, the 62-year-old made clear where he would like the next meeting played: \"There'd be nothing greater than for Fiji to host Ireland in Suva.\" It came ahead of Saturday's Nations Championship clash in Dublin, which Fiji went into bottom of the Southern Hemisphere table, winless from four matches. White, who started the job last month, is focused on making Fiji a more consistent force before next year's World Cup in Australia."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
