      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching pressure",
          "heading": "England's seven-try win over Australia at Twickenham eases pressure on Borthwick",
          "body": "Australia were beaten 45-22 at Allianz Stadium Twickenham, and the BBC framed the result as emphatic on-pitch backing for head coach Steve Borthwick. It was England's Round 4 win in the Nations Championship, and they scored seven tries against what the BBC described as a listless Australia side. Henry Pollock scored two tries after replacing the injured Immanuel Feyi-Waboso at the break, switching to the wing."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales end All Blacks drought with 35-28 win",
          "body": ""
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection tactics",
          "heading": "Rassie Erasmus' front-row swap before France not forbidden by Nations Championship rules",
          "body": "South Africa coach Rassie Erasmus swapped his starting and replacement front rows shortly before the match, and Rugbyrama reports the move was not forbidden by the Nations Championship regulations. Under the rules of the game, teams must name 15 starters and eight replacements 48 hours before the match, with late changes allowed only for injury. Rugbyrama says a match commissioner at the World Cup or Six Nations would not have validated such a change, but this competition's rulebook allows changes to the starting XV in theory possible."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales end All Blacks drought with 35-28 win",
          "body": "England thrash Australia 45-22."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Rugbyrama"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury recall",
          "heading": "Ryan Baird recalls playing on against South Africa with a broken leg",
          "body": "The bang Baird took against South Africa in Dublin last November felt like a dead leg, so he played on. Beirne, he says, told him to come off if he could not run, and an X-ray showed the leg was broken. Baird calls the year that followed “soul-sapping”, but says he came back for two URC games and a Heineken Cup quarter-final."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales end All Blacks drought with 35-28 win",
          "body": "England thrash Australia 45-22."
        }
      ]
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "U20 team news",
          "heading": "Andrea Di Giandomenico named Italy U20 side to face France in Parma",
          "body": "Italy U20 faced France U20 on Friday in the first test of their 2026-27 season, a side blending returning players with newcomers. The 28-man squad gathered at the Cittadella del Rugby in Parma from Monday 9 November, with the aim of bringing younger players into the group. The last meeting, the U20 Six Nations in Lille in February, ended 32-17 to France, with Enoch Opoku Gyamfi shown a 20-minute red card."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
