      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Historic upset",
          "heading": "Wales end 73-year All Blacks wait with 35-28 Principality win",
          "body": "Saturday's Nations Championship win over New Zealand at the Principality Stadium ended a run of 34 straight defeats to the All Blacks, with the last Welsh victory coming in 1953. Wales scored a record five tries, but the defining feature was a defensive effort that held New Zealand over the line five times and produced 341 tackles. Former captain Sam Warburton told ITV it was \"one of the greatest wins in Wales' history.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Australia 45-22",
          "body": ""
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Principality Stadium, Cardiff"
      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection shuffle",
          "heading": "Contepomi shuffles XV, moving Delguy to fullback for Genoa win",
          "body": "Juan Cruz Mallía's sprained knee, suffered against Ireland, forced Felipe Contepomi into a five-change reshuffle for Genoa. Bautista Delguy moved to fullback, Isgró started on the wing and Simón Benítez Cruz came in at scrum-half, while Matera shifted to No. 8 with Scelzo and Moro in the back row. Bautista Bernasconi started at hooker in place of the unavailable Julián Montoya, with Facundo Bosch on the bench. Argentina won 19-14."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales end All Blacks drought with 35-28 win",
          "body": "England thrash Australia 45-22."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
