      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Post-match review",
          "heading": "Wallabies shipped seven tries in 45-22 defeat to England at Allianz Stadium",
          "body": "England crossed for seven tries, with BBC Sport describing Australia as listless on the day. Scrum-half Ryan Lonergan pointed to England's speed in executing their plans, saying they \"really beat us in those areas\". The collision battle, he added, was the main point from the defensive review, and Australia now head to Murrayfield staring at a fourth straight Test defeat."
        },
