    "463": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Player profile",
          "heading": "Warner Dearns recalls reluctant move from New Zealand to Japan at 14",
          "body": "Dearns admits he did not want to move: \"I said I didn't want to go,\" he recalls of the switch from New Zealand's North Island to a city outside Tokyo, when his father took a job at NEC Green Rockets. At Kashiwa Senior High School he switched from basketball to rugby. He qualified on residency grounds and debuted for Japan in November 2021 at 19. This season, on sabbatical, he helped the Hurricanes win their first Super Rugby title in a decade."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales end All Blacks drought with 35-28 win",
          "body": "England thrash Australia 45-22."
        }
      ],
